                <pb facs="0324" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg258"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1631/72a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in El
                        Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-30T19:00:00-04:00">August 30, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Department’s instruction No. 21, July 20, 1934. Please inquire of the
                    Salvadoran Government whether it is prepared to initiate exploratory
                    conversations at an early date. Since this Government is planning to give public
                    notice shortly of the intention to negotiate agreements with other Central
                    American countries it seems appropriate to inquire as a matter of courtesy
                    whether the Salvadoran Government desires a similar announcement to be made with
                    respect to that country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
